      "notes": [
        {
          "text": "The tariff prints overlapping bands ('35001 – 45000' and '45000 and above'); a ship of exactly 45,000 GRT is entered in the 35,001–45,000 band.",
          "source": {
            "document": "tariff-2026-05",
            "page": 1,
            "section": "J-2"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Rates are in USD with no separate coastal rates; the same rates are entered for foreign and coastal ships.",
          "source": {
            "document": "tariff-2026-05",
            "page": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The berth hire minimum is in rupees while the rate is in dollars; the tariff does not say how they combine, so the minimum is not applied.",
          "source": {
            "document": "tariff-2026-05",
            "page": 1,
            "section": "J-6"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Anchorage is per GT per day; the tariff does not say whether a part day counts as a full day, so exact days are used.",
          "source": {
            "document": "tariff-2026-05",
            "page": 2,
            "section": "J-7"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The tariff has no end date; it is entered as in force from 1 May 2026 until a newer tariff is found.",
          "source": {
            "document": "tariff-2026-05",
            "page": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Berth hire is printed 'per GRT per hour' without 'or part thereof', so exact hours are used."
        },
        {
          "text": "Pilotage carries an extra charge by ship age (keel laid), per GRT in USD: 0 for 0-5 years, 0.017744 for 5-10, 0.026616 for 10-15, 0.039924 for 15-20, 0.053232 for 20-25 and 0.0600 for 25 years or more (table J-8). We don't ask for ship age, so it is not added.",
          "source": {
            "document": "tariff-2026-05",
            "page": 2,
            "section": "J-8"
          }
        }
      ]
